  "question": {
    "text": "A metal has a work function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#981;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and its corresponding threshold wavelength is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>. If the threshold wavelength for a metal whose work function is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>&#981;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>, then what is the the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We know,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ϕ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ℏ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></msub></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo>&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ϕ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ϕ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>'</mo></msubsup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>'</mo></msubsup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></math></p><p>Here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ϕ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>'</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ϕ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo>&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>'</mo></msubsup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo>&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>'</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo>&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p>",
